WEBVTT

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:14.000
Hey, is that the design
you thought of yesterday?

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.790
Whoa! Please don't scare me like that.

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:19.620
What? I would buy it.

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:21.540
I like what you did.

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:24.950
Th-Thank you very much.

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:27.580
Actually, I'm proud of what I did here.

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:28.450
Cool.

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:29.410
Huh?

00:00:29.410 --> 00:00:32.580
I bet Miss Sara would like it, too.

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:38.290
Hey, Chiyuki.

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:41.580
When did you become so close
with the bean sprouts guy?

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:43.200
Bean sprouts...?

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.080
Ah, you mean Ikuto!

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:46.580
Ikuto...?

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:48.870
Do we seem that close?

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:50.700
Well, I guess we are close.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:53.830
We are... But I wouldn't call us friends.

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:55.290
Oh...

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:58.660
I actually respect Ikuto quite a bit.

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:00.330
What?

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:04.790
I'm dead serious about becoming a hypermodel.

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:08.660
If something's not relevant to modeling,
I cut it out of my life.

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:11.620
But... Ikuto's not like that.

00:01:11.620 --> 00:01:14.120
He never abandons anything.
He takes care of it all.

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:16.040
"Ichika"
He's had his dream longer than I've had mine.

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:19.000
He's had his dream longer than I've had mine.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:23.620
But it's not because he's not
putting in enough effort.

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:29.120
He's got the determination to find
the right balance without abandoning anything.

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:30.750
That's something I don't have.

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:36.000
It's impressive, and I respect him for it,

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:38.450
but I also see him as a rival.

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:41.660
That's why... Ikuto...

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:43.370
...you have to win.

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:47.000
Or else, you won't be able
to prove your efforts.

00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:13.290
"Smile Down the Runway"

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:19.870
"Episode 6: Superiority and Inferiority"
Time's up!

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:22.870
"Episode 6: Superiority and Inferiority"
Let's move on to the evaluations.

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:24.950
I... did it...

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:27.790
You're... a high school student?

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:30.120
Oh... Yes...

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:31.040
Kaoru Kizaki.

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:31.950
Ah.

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:33.750
You're up first.

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:39.450
Now that it's time to evaluate,
let me introduce our judges.

00:03:39.450 --> 00:03:44.290
First, our principal, Shoko Takaoka.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:46.580
Good evening!

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:47.750
And also...

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:50.910
...the faculty in charge, which is me. And...

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:57.080
...three fellow competitors in this room,
a total of five judges.

00:03:57.080 --> 00:04:00.830
The first three are Tsumura, Kato, and Yajima.

00:04:00.830 --> 00:04:02.660
Come on up front.

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:06.000
We're... the judges?!

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.200
Excuse me.

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:11.620
I'd rather not be evaluated by
someone with inferior skills than me.

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:15.830
Oh my, he hasn't shown up yet?!

00:04:15.830 --> 00:04:18.540
Huh? Who's "he"?

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:20.120
Hey there.

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:22.620
You got me worried, Toh!

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:26.250
Kaoru, do you have any objections now?

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:29.000
Oh... No.

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:30.540
"An amazing outfit for Sara"

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:35.120
"An amazing outfit for Sara"
When you're presenting,
start off with your design's concept.

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:37.750
Yes.

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:41.080
My concept is... "Unbalance."

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:44.660
What stood out to me most when researching
Sara was how different she is on TV

00:04:44.660 --> 00:04:47.750
compared to when she is modeling.

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:50.830
While cool and reserved,
she's also warm and lovable.

00:04:50.830 --> 00:04:55.500
I wanted to portray that
by juxtaposing leather and lace.

00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:57.660
Yajima, critique her.

00:04:57.660 --> 00:05:00.950
What?! I'm first?

00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:02.870
Yeah, we don't have all day here.

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:09.250
Well, the concept is interesting,
but I think it looks a bit lame...

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:11.000
Here we go.

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:14.290
The preliminaries are all about
roasting each other after all.

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:16.330
--They exaggerate every flaw they can find.

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:18.620
--I think it's a great design.
--They exaggerate every flaw they can find.

00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:21.660
Um... Will you show us the backside?

00:05:24.580 --> 00:05:27.080
See? Isn't it elegant?

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:31.870
The lace on the back tones down
the ruggedness of the leather.

00:05:31.870 --> 00:05:34.410
Who does he think he is?
He's just a high schooler.

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:36.330
I admire her handling of leather.

00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:36.910
What?!

00:05:36.910 --> 00:05:38.540
I like it, too.

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:43.580
You were meticulous with your fabric choice,
and it would look great on Sara.

00:05:43.580 --> 00:05:44.830
Yes!

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:48.500
Next, Ryunosuke Eda.

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:52.660
I don't have a particular concept
in mind at all.

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:56.040
As a professional, it's her job
to make it look good.

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:57.580
It screams out "tracht" to me.

00:05:57.580 --> 00:05:58.450
Ah.

00:05:58.450 --> 00:06:03.620
Tracht is a traditional garment of Switzerland,
which is part of Sara's background.

00:06:03.620 --> 00:06:07.080
It's impressive how he
incorporated that in his design.

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:09.200
The design is plain lame.

00:06:09.200 --> 00:06:12.250
I recognize all the trends,
but they don't work together.

00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:15.540
I don't get why it had to be a turtleneck.

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:17.500
Everyone's so harsh.

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:18.870
It's almost my turn...

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:21.000
Next, Ikuto Tsumura.

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:22.160
Yes!

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:23.620
As for the judges...

00:06:23.620 --> 00:06:26.580
Excuse me... May I be a judge?

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:28.040
Then, me too!

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:32.330
All right Tsumura. Let's see it.

00:06:32.330 --> 00:06:34.080
Yes.

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:36.000
This is what I designed.

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:40.040
Pajamas!

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:40.250
--Huh?!

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:41.700
--Huh?!
--Huh?!

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:43.830
Pajamas...?

00:06:43.830 --> 00:06:46.410
Yes... Pajamas!

00:06:48.910 --> 00:06:50.620
Tell me, why pajamas?

00:06:50.620 --> 00:06:56.330
Miss Sara said it herself. "Every girl
wants to look stylish all the time."

00:06:56.330 --> 00:07:01.700
I noticed how she posts her outfits
on social media every day.

00:07:01.700 --> 00:07:04.620
But there aren't many posts
of her wearing lounge wear.

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:10.540
That's why I designed pajamas that would
make her excited about posting on social media.

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:16.250
So tell me, what part of that design is stylish?

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:19.120
What? You mean it's not stylish at all...?

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:23.790
Oh, no... How can I convince
you that it's stylish...?

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:25.540
U-Um...

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:28.370
You've improved a lot, Ikuto.

00:07:28.370 --> 00:07:35.410
In order to achieve this form, you mastered
the bias-cut you struggled with before.

00:07:35.410 --> 00:07:38.660
I'll start with the critique.

00:07:38.660 --> 00:07:42.040
Honestly... I'm disappointed.

00:07:42.040 --> 00:07:44.580
Everything about it is half-hearted.

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:48.200
From the positioning of the buttons
to the length of the hem...

00:07:48.200 --> 00:07:51.660
It's too conservative--it offends me.

00:07:51.660 --> 00:07:53.830
It's lame.

00:07:53.830 --> 00:07:55.250
Lame...?

00:07:57.620 --> 00:07:58.700
Now.

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:04.160
We'll select the participants who will proceed
to the next round. But, before that...

00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:06.370
We'll give you some time to fix things up.

00:08:06.370 --> 00:08:07.250
What?

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:13.290
If you wish to submit your design without
a fix-up, meet us at Multipurpose Room A.

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:17.870
What...

00:08:17.870 --> 00:08:19.830
...should I do...?

00:08:19.830 --> 00:08:22.080
Hey, Ikuto.

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:24.580
I would buy it.

00:08:25.910 --> 00:08:28.700
I like what you did there.

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:32.620
"Multipurpose Room A"

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:42.450
Oh, you didn't fix up your lame pajamas?

00:08:42.450 --> 00:08:44.790
Who cares. That's his choice.

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:46.700
U-Um...

00:08:46.700 --> 00:08:48.290
Thank you very much.

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:49.540
Huh?

00:08:49.540 --> 00:08:53.660
I was grateful that time before
the preliminaries, too...

00:08:53.660 --> 00:08:55.040
Whatever...

00:08:59.160 --> 00:09:00.700
Miss Kokoro!

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:04.450
Everyone, thanks for waiting!

00:09:04.450 --> 00:09:11.000
The task was to make a stylish outfit for Sara.

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:14.750
Some of you were told your designs were lame.

00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:22.700
But actually... There's nothing more subjective
about deeming something as stylish or not.

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:26.540
But what's more important for the designer
when it comes to making clothes

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:31.370
is whether the design is interesting or not.

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:35.080
Therefore, the true task of this round

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:41.870
was to see whether you were able to believe in
your design, even after all the harsh critiques.

00:09:41.870 --> 00:09:42.790
Ah!

00:09:42.790 --> 00:09:45.700
So, thank you all for your interesting designs!

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:49.250
Congratulations, you all passed the first round!

00:09:49.250 --> 00:09:52.000
I... passed...?

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:55.120
But that's not all...

00:09:55.120 --> 00:09:59.120
We're about to reveal
the top 3 out of 18 participants

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:03.700
who will get to proceed straight to
the finals from here.

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:08.910
Or else, why would we be here as judges?

00:10:08.910 --> 00:10:12.830
The finals... To participate
in the fashion show!

00:10:19.290 --> 00:10:25.120
Toh, did Ikuto's design
really bother you that much?

00:10:25.120 --> 00:10:26.830
No, not at all.

00:10:26.830 --> 00:10:28.870
What did you think, Shoko?

00:10:28.870 --> 00:10:33.000
Sara adores stripes, you know?

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:37.500
So if he knew that, he possesses

00:10:37.500 --> 00:10:43.660
something great that allows him to really
tailor the design to the client's taste.

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:48.950
Yes!

00:10:53.450 --> 00:10:56.790
I lost... after all...

00:10:56.790 --> 00:11:01.000
Mr. Ikuto! Congratulations on making top three!

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:02.620
It's true...

00:11:02.620 --> 00:11:06.450
I never expected to be ranked so high.

00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:10.790
I don't understand!
Why am I ranked lower than this kid?!

00:11:10.790 --> 00:11:11.950
Oh...

00:11:11.950 --> 00:11:13.790
It's rather simple.

00:11:13.790 --> 00:11:17.120
Your process wasn't suited for women's clothing.

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:20.620
It's fine to challenge yourself
with an unfamiliar category...

00:11:20.620 --> 00:11:23.160
But if that were the case,
you should've done your homework.

00:11:25.790 --> 00:11:27.410
Damn it...

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:32.580
--Hey.
--Huh?

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:35.830
He left without getting any information
on the second round.

00:11:35.830 --> 00:11:38.660
What a shame. He's got great potential.

00:11:38.660 --> 00:11:44.540
Well, I'll be staying for the information
session. Have a great evening.

00:11:44.790 --> 00:11:47.200
"Geika Fashion School"

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:49.580
"Calling... Chiyuki Fujito"

00:11:50.540 --> 00:11:52.120
She's not picking up.

00:11:52.120 --> 00:11:54.750
Hey, you're still here.

00:11:54.750 --> 00:11:57.080
Oh... Um...

00:11:57.080 --> 00:11:59.750
I wanted to wait for Miss Kokoro.

00:11:59.750 --> 00:12:05.910
Tell me, Ikuto. Are you satisfied
with the preliminary's results?

00:12:05.910 --> 00:12:09.370
I'm not really sure...

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:12.500
I don't think I am satisfied.

00:12:12.500 --> 00:12:13.450
But...

00:12:13.450 --> 00:12:17.500
You made a crucial mistake.
Why didn't you spend all of your budget?

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:20.540
What? How could you tell?

00:12:20.540 --> 00:12:23.910
I could tell right away
just by looking at the fabric.

00:12:23.910 --> 00:12:28.080
So it's no wonder you lost this time.

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:30.290
You've got it all wrong!

00:12:30.290 --> 00:12:32.830
Even so,

00:12:32.830 --> 00:12:34.370
it's still not acceptable.

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:42.620
You prioritized personal reasons over
achieving the finest quality design possible,

00:12:42.620 --> 00:12:45.660
which is an insincere act as a designer.

00:12:45.660 --> 00:12:47.330
I'll say it loud and clear.

00:12:47.330 --> 00:12:55.040
You failed today because you were stingy
with the fabric. No matter the reason,

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:57.910
it shouldn't affect the client, ever.

00:13:00.660 --> 00:13:04.290
But I had no choice...

00:13:04.290 --> 00:13:09.580
That money belonged to my sisters...

00:13:09.580 --> 00:13:16.750
I'm the first-born son! If I need
to use my sisters' money... I...

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:24.290
I admire how you didn't finish that thought...

00:13:25.250 --> 00:13:30.450
Sorry, I didn't mean to lecture you.

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:32.580
But Ikuto...

00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:39.790
You're going to have to make full-size outfits
for the finals. You'll need more money.

00:13:39.790 --> 00:13:41.410
Oh...

00:13:41.410 --> 00:13:45.330
You're not making enough
working at Hajime's, right?

00:13:46.830 --> 00:13:49.540
Then...

00:13:49.540 --> 00:13:51.870
Why don't you come work for me?

00:13:51.870 --> 00:13:53.330
What...?

00:13:53.330 --> 00:13:59.290
Not for Mai Ayano's brand. I mean, for my brand.

00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:04.580
<i>Smile Down the Runway</i>.

00:14:04.910 --> 00:14:08.870
"Geika Fashion School"
What?! You're launching your own brand?!

00:14:08.870 --> 00:14:11.250
"Geika Fashion School"
That's right! Pretty soon, now.

00:14:11.250 --> 00:14:12.660
That's amazing.

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:15.540
But what about Aphro I Dite...?

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:17.160
I'm going to quit.

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:21.870
I'm allowed to become independent
once my grandmother approves of my abilities.

00:14:21.870 --> 00:14:23.870
Oh...

00:14:23.870 --> 00:14:28.250
I've lived my life for this moment.

00:14:28.250 --> 00:14:31.500
I need more money for the finals.

00:14:33.370 --> 00:14:39.620
Um... Then... May I please work for you...?

00:14:40.790 --> 00:14:42.330
He's not picking up.

00:14:42.330 --> 00:14:43.580
Ouch.

00:14:43.580 --> 00:14:48.000
Here. That's all the application forms
for the magazines you requested.

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:50.500
I appreciate it, Shizuku.

00:14:54.200 --> 00:14:56.410
Oh, no...

00:14:56.410 --> 00:15:00.950
Can I cheat my height
just a little... Like 2 cm?

00:15:00.950 --> 00:15:03.000
Forget it, they'll catch you.

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:08.000
I can't even be a fashion magazine model...
Oh, Paris Fashion Week...

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:09.620
How pathetic.

00:15:09.620 --> 00:15:10.540
Ugh...

00:15:10.540 --> 00:15:11.250
"Remaining Balance: 450,789 Yen"

00:15:11.250 --> 00:15:14.000
"Remaining Balance: 450,789 Yen"
Chiyuki, are you really going to Paris?

00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:14.950
"Remaining Balance: 450,789 Yen"
I am.

00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:20.370
Jeez... So how long did it
take you to save that much?

00:15:20.370 --> 00:15:22.910
It took... two years.

00:15:22.910 --> 00:15:24.790
You're going to waste those
two years in an instant.

00:15:24.790 --> 00:15:30.450
It's not a waste-- Could you not
be all negative in front of me?!

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:34.000
Sure... Do what you want.

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:38.750
Anyway, I'm going to apply to
as many magazines as possible.

00:15:38.750 --> 00:15:43.700
All right! Let's start with updating
my comp card and portfolio!

00:15:43.700 --> 00:15:47.580
Shizuku, do you think Miwa
is busy this month...?

00:15:47.580 --> 00:15:50.120
Oh... She's gone.

00:15:50.120 --> 00:15:50.950
I'm here.

00:15:50.950 --> 00:15:52.250
Whoa!

00:15:52.250 --> 00:15:54.500
If you're making a portfolio,

00:15:54.500 --> 00:15:58.660
could you be this girl's mentor?

00:15:58.660 --> 00:16:03.580
My name is Haruka Sudo, and I'm working
for Mille Neige starting today!

00:16:03.580 --> 00:16:05.790
It's an honor to meet you.

00:16:05.790 --> 00:16:07.200
A newcomer?

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:09.950
A newcomer. She's a year younger than you.

00:16:09.950 --> 00:16:12.250
How adorable. It's great to meet you.

00:16:12.250 --> 00:16:14.250
Oh, please...!

00:16:14.250 --> 00:16:17.660
You're infinite times more adorable,
Miss Chiyuki!

00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:21.080
Shoot, I already exposed my fangirl self.

00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:25.160
A fangirl...? I was never that
well-known for my work.

00:16:25.160 --> 00:16:26.500
But you are!

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:31.410
When I was in elementary school, I used to
read magazines with you on the cover!

00:16:31.410 --> 00:16:34.410
I've been a huge fan ever since!

00:16:34.410 --> 00:16:36.040
I see.

00:16:36.040 --> 00:16:38.910
I used to be in more demand, back then.

00:16:40.250 --> 00:16:43.790
Then, let's start with the workflow process.

00:16:43.790 --> 00:16:48.500
Basically, models have to
find work for themselves.

00:16:48.500 --> 00:16:55.000
You fill out applications, get accepted to
audition, then pass the audition to get the job.

00:16:55.000 --> 00:16:59.370
To do that, you need to create
your comp card and portfolio.

00:17:01.120 --> 00:17:04.250
There she is! How's it going, Chi?

00:17:04.250 --> 00:17:08.580
Miwa! Thanks for squeezing me in!

00:17:08.580 --> 00:17:12.910
So, how should we do this today?

00:17:12.910 --> 00:17:18.370
A comp card is basically a promo photo
to include with your application paperwork.

00:17:18.370 --> 00:17:23.500
A portfolio is a stock of photos needed
for you to pass your audition.

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:30.250
You gather together photos with different looks
to sell yourself as the best model.

00:17:30.250 --> 00:17:33.830
Unfortunately, this all comes out
of your own pocket.

00:17:33.830 --> 00:17:37.450
Nice... All right, next!

00:17:37.450 --> 00:17:40.040
What should I wear...?

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:42.700
This one!

00:17:44.370 --> 00:17:46.290
Oh?

00:17:46.290 --> 00:17:48.540
Another unique one.

00:17:50.620 --> 00:17:52.450
Not bad, right?

00:17:53.540 --> 00:17:56.660
At that time...

00:17:56.660 --> 00:18:00.870
I used to put on airs, lie,
and cause all sorts of trouble.

00:18:02.250 --> 00:18:05.700
Where did that outfit come from?

00:18:05.700 --> 00:18:11.290
But things are different now.
I want everyone to see Ikuto's work!

00:18:13.370 --> 00:18:17.410
My friend made it for me.

00:18:19.040 --> 00:18:20.450
Oh, my...

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:24.450
What a lovely face...

00:18:26.500 --> 00:18:29.200
Rejected by every single one!

00:18:29.200 --> 00:18:32.370
Then... I'll just have to call them directly!

00:18:32.370 --> 00:18:36.700
I just have to keep doing everything I can.

00:18:39.700 --> 00:18:41.370
Oh...

00:18:41.370 --> 00:18:44.750
Hello, this is Niinuma of <i>MODE JAPAN</i>.

00:18:44.750 --> 00:18:50.750
Hello, my name is Chiyuki Fujito,
a model from Mille Neige.

00:18:50.750 --> 00:18:52.790
I'm wondering if I can send over
my portfolio for you to review.

00:18:52.790 --> 00:18:54.200
"Chiyuki Fujito"
I'm wondering if I can send over
my portfolio for you to review.

00:18:54.200 --> 00:18:56.370
Would that be all right?

00:18:56.370 --> 00:18:59.040
Just a moment, please.

00:18:59.040 --> 00:19:00.120
Huh?

00:19:02.540 --> 00:19:05.500
The name sounds familiar...

00:19:05.500 --> 00:19:06.290
Ah!

00:19:06.290 --> 00:19:08.000
"Mille Neige Chiyuki Fujito"
Ah!

00:19:08.450 --> 00:19:09.950
Oh!

00:19:09.950 --> 00:19:11.620
Yes!

00:19:11.620 --> 00:19:13.450
I'd love to see it!

00:19:19.040 --> 00:19:21.120
I finally got this far.

00:19:22.160 --> 00:19:24.830
Now it's all about selling myself.

00:19:25.790 --> 00:19:28.000
Hello, are you Ms. Chiyuki Fujito?

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:31.250
Yes, I'm Chiyuki Fujito of Mille Neige.

00:19:31.250 --> 00:19:32.580
Thank you for meeting me today.

00:19:32.580 --> 00:19:34.450
What? You're tiny!

00:19:34.450 --> 00:19:36.080
Oh...

00:19:36.080 --> 00:19:37.620
Well...

00:19:37.620 --> 00:19:40.500
Niinuma had to run to a last-minute location.

00:19:40.500 --> 00:19:44.250
I'm Akasaka. I will take her place today.

00:19:45.120 --> 00:19:48.660
It's not Ms. Niinuma...

00:19:48.660 --> 00:19:53.040
I've got another appointment,
so let's make this quick.

00:19:53.040 --> 00:19:54.580
Darn it...

00:19:54.580 --> 00:19:57.370
I had my hopes up.

00:19:57.370 --> 00:20:01.750
No eye contact... Cold words...

00:20:01.750 --> 00:20:03.250
Nothing new.

00:20:04.500 --> 00:20:06.000
Pull yourself together!

00:20:09.000 --> 00:20:14.700
Hey, you don't look too tiny in these photos.

00:20:14.700 --> 00:20:19.330
Yes, my proportions are pretty much
the same as a top model.

00:20:19.330 --> 00:20:23.540
So as long as it's a static image,
it wouldn't negatively affect the brand image.

00:20:23.540 --> 00:20:28.580
I may not be useful when the photo
is composed of multiple models,

00:20:28.580 --> 00:20:32.330
but will you take a look at page 20?

00:20:32.330 --> 00:20:34.000
Okay...

00:20:35.830 --> 00:20:37.660
Where is this?

00:20:37.660 --> 00:20:41.080
I arranged a shoot in a forest.

00:20:41.080 --> 00:20:46.950
I hear high fashion brands value synergy
with the shoot's location nowadays.

00:20:46.950 --> 00:20:50.830
I'm capable of adapting to all sorts
of different environments.

00:20:50.830 --> 00:20:54.660
So if you can please consider me...

00:20:54.660 --> 00:20:57.330
How's her reaction...?

00:20:57.330 --> 00:20:58.370
It shouldn't be that bad.

00:20:58.370 --> 00:20:59.620
Oh.

00:20:59.620 --> 00:21:01.250
Ah!

00:21:01.250 --> 00:21:02.700
What?

00:21:02.700 --> 00:21:05.620
Ms. Fujito, I have to end our appointment here.

00:21:05.620 --> 00:21:09.370
Ms. Igarashi, I apologize for the wait.

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:16.910
A manager from an agency...?

00:21:16.910 --> 00:21:19.200
This is the worst timing ever...

00:21:20.700 --> 00:21:23.410
Ms. Akasaka, if you'd like, I can meet again...

00:21:23.410 --> 00:21:25.370
Please contact us another day.

00:21:31.540 --> 00:21:34.540
I will contact you tonight to follow-up.

00:21:37.450 --> 00:21:38.790
Who's she?

00:21:38.790 --> 00:21:44.830
She's a model from Mille Neige
who's looking for work.

00:21:46.450 --> 00:21:47.950
I see.

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:55.660
And of course... no answer.

00:21:55.660 --> 00:21:58.870
What did I expect? It's nothing new.

00:21:58.870 --> 00:22:00.160
Whoa!

00:22:00.160 --> 00:22:02.500
Yes! Hello?

00:22:02.500 --> 00:22:05.250
Hello, this is Akasaka of <i>MODE JAPAN</i>.

00:22:05.250 --> 00:22:09.330
I'm wondering if you were
available tomorrow morning?

00:22:09.330 --> 00:22:10.200
What?

00:22:10.200 --> 00:22:15.290
A model dropped out at the last minute,
so I'm wondering if you can join the shoot.

00:22:15.290 --> 00:22:16.750
Oh...

00:22:22.040 --> 00:22:24.790
Good morning.

00:22:29.750 --> 00:22:33.580
Whoa...! I'm sorry.

00:22:33.580 --> 00:22:34.660
Oh.

00:22:35.660 --> 00:22:37.620
What?

00:22:37.620 --> 00:22:40.540
I'm sorry, Ms. Igarashi!

00:22:40.540 --> 00:22:42.370
I'm late again.

00:22:45.620 --> 00:22:47.200
Wow...

00:22:48.870 --> 00:22:53.000
The star of today's shoot...

00:22:53.000 --> 00:22:54.370
So beautiful.

00:22:58.950 --> 00:23:00.370
...is her.

00:24:31.580 --> 00:24:33.950
Next, "Aura."

00:24:33.950 --> 00:24:36.910
"See you next time!!"
